meta {
  name: Send Message
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/chats/{{chatId}}/messages
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Origin: {{clientUrl}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "content": "What did I write about deployment?"
  }
}

docs {
  Stores the question. Generating the answer is not wired up yet — that arrives
  with the streaming work, and the reply will come over the socket rather than
  in this response.

  content is trimmed, and capped at 4000 characters. A long paste belongs in a
  note: anything sent here is billed as input again on every later turn of the
  conversation.

  Three guards run in order — the chat must be yours, the traffic reasonable,
  and the AI budget not exhausted. A refusal for budget returns 429 with
  Retry-After set to when your oldest charge ages out of the rolling window, and
  writes nothing, so a refused question leaves no trace in the chat.
}
